{
  "_comment": "MSP-B1 offline fixture for the native AWS event connector. Each scope's `events` are RAW provider payloads in the NATIVE shapes the MSP-B0 mappers consume (CloudWatch/EventBridge Alarm State Change envelopes, EventBridge event envelopes, CloudTrail records) \u2014 NOT the DescribeAlarmHistory export shapes used by the B8 export loaders. TWO accounts are seeded so the offline path exercises the MSP 'one connection, many accounts, each account a scope' model (AC1). Recurrence volumes are deliberate: each recurring signature fires 6x, which clears the B7 noise floor of 5 for the state_change/audit/access classes (discovery/signals/ops_calibration.py) so offline runs actually reach the Cloud Operations detectors instead of being suppressed as noise \u2014 while still demonstrating B7 admission folding the re-fires into ONE active signal with a count. The denied TerminateInstances event is event_class 'error', which is never floored. LIVE DATA NEEDED: this file is a demo estate only; a live run polls the customer's real accounts declared in AWS_EVENT_ACCOUNTS or pinned on the aws_events Integration Hub connector record.",
